Z||000001||fieroman_5000||11-21-2001||10:15 PM||||My '84 SE has wool seats??? I've seen alot of pics of other '84 interiors and all of them hade the material seats. Is this option?? The wool runs down the middle and there is leather along the sides.<P>Fieroman <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||11-21-2001||10:18 PM||||The suede leather with wool inserts was an option in 84. I think it was 84 only year it was available.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||11-21-2001||11:09 PM||||I don't think that's wool..... it's probably mold....you need to air out your car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Seriously, I saw a pair of them at the junkyard and they were all moldy and had moss growing on them...yuk! I think they're pretty rare.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fieroman_5000||11-21-2001||11:19 PM||||On the passenger side seat the wool is kinda weird...as though some of it has come off in little chunks. Do you think there is any way of repairing them w/o taking it to a recovering person?<P>Fieroman <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||ITB 2M4||11-22-2001||02:34 AM||||Supposedly, they only came on '84's that were 'showroom' cars.  I had a set on my '84, but sold them to a guy with an '87 GT.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4||||reg||1
Z||000006||fieroman_5000||11-22-2001||11:57 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ITB 2M4:<BR><B>Supposedly, they only came on '84's that were 'showroom' cars.  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>WOW! really??? never heard of that. So i guess i should restore then? <P>Fieroman <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||mrfiero||11-22-2001||03:06 PM||||The fleece and suede seats were a level 3 option on '84 SE's and '85 SE & GT models.  <P>They are pretty rare and all are generally in poor shape....they are very high maintenance seats.  <P>If your suede parts are in good shape then you should be able to replace the fleece inserts, but you will have to remove and disassemble the seats to do it.  I couldn't tell you what it would cost, but I imagine that the fleece woulod be pricey. <P>Your other option would be to scour junkyards.....the passenger sides are normally in better shape than the drivers side, so you could reskin your seats with 2 good passenger seats.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||REDHOTT88||11-22-2001||08:55 PM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by fieroman_5000:<BR>[B]On the passenger side seat the wool is kinda weird...as though some of it has come off in little chunks. Do you think there is any way of repairing them w/o taking it to a recovering person?<P>I agree with rockcrawl, that probably is mold. The reason it looks weird and is coming of in chunks is because the sun probably got to it there. (needs moist, darkness.) You'll have to go to the local greenhouse and buy some more moss seeds and replant. Better yet, go to a junkyard and scrape off some existing mold for a better color match!<P>Just kidding! I never heard of such a thing...<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>1988 Formula (red & shiny allover)- and she doesn't like to wear a bra!||||reg||1
